/?           List help topics or read about one topic.

 HELP [topic]

   topic           Command, driver or CONFIG.SYS directive to look up.

 Omit the topic to browse the index. Use /? on supported commands
 to display the same help page.
ANSI.SYS     Add ANSI console support.

 DEVICE=ANSI.SYS [/X] [/L] [/K]

   /X              Allow extended keys to be redefined.
   /L              Keep the line count when switching modes.
   /K              Use the conventional keyboard interface.

 Console sequences start with ESC (ASCII 27) followed by [.
   row;colH        Position the cursor (top left is 1;1).
   6n              Report cursor position as ESC[row;colR.
   2J, K           Clear the screen, or clear to the end of the line.
APPEND       Search additional directories when opening data files.

 APPEND [path[;path...]] [/X[:ON|OFF]] [/PATH:ON|OFF] [/E]

   path            Search directories, separated by semicolons.
   /X              Use appended paths for more file operations.
   /PATH:ON        Search appended paths even if the name includes a path.
   /PATH:OFF       Search appended paths only for names without a path.
   /E              Store the list in the environment.

 Run APPEND to display the current list. Use APPEND ; to clear it.
ASSIGN       Redirect drive letters.

 ASSIGN [x=y ...]
 ASSIGN /STATUS | /STA

   x=y             Redirect drive x to drive y. Colons are optional (B:=A:).
   /STATUS, /STA   List current assignments.

 A mapping with /STATUS applies the mapping. Run /STATUS alone to list it.
 Run ASSIGN without arguments to remove all assignments.
ATTRIB       Display or change file attributes.

 ATTRIB [+R|-R] [+A|-A] [+H|-H] [+S|-S] filespec [/S]
 ATTRIB filespec name[=value] [/S]

   +R, -R          Set or clear the read-only attribute.
   +A, -A          Set or clear the archive attribute.
   +H, -H          Set or clear the hidden attribute.
   +S, -S          Set or clear the system attribute.
                   Clear existing hidden and system bits to change other flags.
   filespec        Required file or wildcard pattern.
   name            FILESIZE, DATE and TIME display read-only file information.
                   Other named attributes require filesystem support. Use *
                   for the list of names, or name=value to set a writable one.
   /S              Include matching files in subdirectories.
BACKUP       Back up files to another disk.

 BACKUP source target [/S] [/M] [/A] [/D:date] [/T:time]
        [/L[:logfile]] [/F[:size]]

   source          Files to back up.
   target          Backup drive.
   /S              Include subdirectories.
   /M              Select changed files.
   /A              Append to a backup.
   /D:date         Filter by modification date (four-digit year).
   /T:time         Filter by modification time.
   /L[:logfile]    Log backup activity.
   /F[:size]       Format media at the given capacity.
BREAK        Control extended Ctrl+C checking.

 BREAK [ON|OFF]

   ON, OFF         Enable or disable extended Ctrl+C checking.

 Run BREAK alone to display the current setting.
BREAK=       Enable or disable extended Ctrl+C checking.

 BREAK=ON
 BREAK=OFF
BUFFERS=     Set the number of disk buffers.

 BUFFERS=count[,secondary] [/X] [/L]

   count           Disk buffers to allocate at startup.
   secondary       Secondary buffer count (0-8).
   /X              Try expanded memory first.
   /L              Use conventional memory if EMS is unused or unavailable.
CALL         Run a nested batch file.

 CALL batchfile [arguments]

   batchfile       Batch file to run.
   arguments       Arguments for the nested batch file.
CD           Show or change the current directory.

 CD [drive:][path]

   drive           Drive to inspect or change the directory on.
   path            New current directory. Use .. for its parent.

 Run CD alone to display the current directory.
CHCP         Display or change the active code page.

 CHCP [codepage]

   codepage        Code page number to activate.

 Run CHCP alone to display the active code page.
CHDIR        Show or change the current directory.

 CHDIR [drive:][path]

   drive           Drive to inspect or change the directory on.
   path            New current directory. Use .. for its parent.

 Run CD alone to display the current directory.
CHKDSK       Check a disk and report its condition.

 CHKDSK [drive:][path] [/F] [/V]

   drive           Disk to check.
   path            File or pattern to examine for fragmentation.
   /F              Repair disk errors.
   /V              Display filenames while checking.
CLS          Clear the display.

 CLS
COMMAND      Start another command interpreter.

 COMMAND [drive:][path] [device] [/E:size] [/P [/MSG]] [/D] [/F] [/C command]

   [drive:][path]  Directory containing COMMAND.COM.
   device          Console character device.
   /E:size         Environment size in bytes (160 to 32768).
                   DOS rounds up to a multiple of 16.
   /P              Start a permanent interpreter. EXIT cannot close it.
   /MSG            With /P, retain extended error messages.
   /D              Skip startup date and time prompts.
   /F              Return Fail automatically on critical errors.
   /C command      Run the remaining command line and exit.
COMMENT=     Change the CONFIG.SYS comment character.

 COMMENT=character

   character       CONFIG.SYS comment character.
COMP         Compare files.

 COMP file1 file2 [/D] [/A] [/L] [/N=n] [/C]

   file1, file2    Files or file groups to compare.
   /D              Display differing bytes in decimal.
   /A              Display differing bytes as characters.
   /L              Identify differences by line number.
   /N=n            Compare the first n lines.
   /C              Ignore case.
COPY         Copy files or combine several files into one.

 COPY source[+source...] [destination] [/A | /B] [/V] [/Y | /-Y]

   source       File to copy. Join names with + to combine files.
   destination  Name or directory for the copy.
   /A           Treat the file as text.
   /B           Treat the file as binary.
   /V           Verify writes.
   /Y           Overwrite without prompting.
   /-Y          Ask before overwriting.

 COPYCMD sets the default overwrite behavior. The last explicit switch wins.
COUNTRY.SYS  Country data selected by the CONFIG.SYS COUNTRY= directive.

 COUNTRY=country[,codepage][,filename]

   filename        Country data file specified in CONFIG.SYS.
COUNTRY=     Select country and code-page information.

 COUNTRY=country[,codepage][,filename]

   country         Country code for regional conventions.
   codepage        Code page to use.
   filename        Country data file path.
CPSW=        Configure code-page switching.

 CPSW=ON
 CPSW=OFF
CTTY         Change the command interpreter console.

 CTTY device

   device          Character device for console input and output.

 Use CTTY CON to select the local console.
DATE         Display or set the date.

 DATE [date]

   date            New date in country order, with a four-digit year (1980-2099).
DEBUG        Inspect and modify memory and run machine-code programs.

 DEBUG [filename [arguments]]

   filename        Program or file to debug.
   arguments       Program arguments.

 At the DEBUG prompt, type ? for a command list.
DEL          Delete one or more files.

 DEL [drive:][path]filename [/P] [/Q]

   filename        File or wildcard pattern to delete.
   /P              Ask before deleting each file.
   /Q              Skip the bulk deletion prompt.
DELTREE      Delete a directory tree.

 DELTREE [/Y] path [path...]

   path            File or tree to delete. Wildcards allowed.
   /Y              Delete each target without prompting.

 Roots, . and .. cannot be selected as targets.
DEVICE=      Load a device driver with optional arguments.

 DEVICE=filename [arguments]

   filename        Device driver path.
   arguments       Driver options.
DEVICEHIGH=  Load a driver in upper memory when space permits.

 DEVICEHIGH=filename [arguments]

   filename        Device driver path.
   arguments       Driver options.

 DOS uses conventional memory if the driver cannot load high.
DIR          List files and subdirectories.

 DIR [path] [/2Y] [/A[:attrs]] [/B] [/L] [/O[:order]] [/P] [/S] [/W]

   /2Y             Display two-digit years (legacy layout).

   path        Drive, directory or filename pattern to list.
   /A          Select entries by attribute. Prefix a letter with - to exclude.
                 D  Directory     R  Read-only     H  Hidden
                 S  System        A  Archive
   /O          Sort entries. Prefix a key with - to reverse its order.
                 N  Name          E  Extension     S  Size
                 D  Date          G  Directories first
   /P          Pause after each screen.
   /W          Use wide format.
   /S          Include subdirectories.
   /B          Show bare names.
   /L          Show lowercase names.

 Set defaults with DIRCMD. For example, /-W cancels a preset /W.
DISKCOMP     Compare two floppy disks.

 DISKCOMP [drive1:] [drive2:] [/1] [/8]

   drive1, drive2  Drives holding the disks to compare.
   /1              Compare only the first side.
   /8              Compare only the first eight sectors of each track.

 An omitted drive defaults to the current drive.
 With one drive, insert each disk when prompted.
DISKCOPY     Copy a floppy disk.

 DISKCOPY [drive1:] [drive2:] [/1] [/V]

   drive1          Source drive.
   drive2          Destination drive.
   /1              Copy only the first side.
   /V              Verify the destination tracks.

 An omitted drive defaults to the current drive.
 Copying overwrites the destination disk. Swap disks when prompted.
DISPLAY.SYS  Install display code-page support.

 DEVICE=DISPLAY.SYS CON[:]=(type[,hwcp[,n]])

   type            Display adapter type.
   hwcp            Hardware code page, optionally in parentheses.
   n               Software code-page slots. Also accepts (n,m).
DOS=         Select high memory and upper memory support.

 DOS=HIGH,UMB

   HIGH            Move selected DOS routines into the high memory area.
   UMB             Enable upper memory blocks.

 Specify either setting alone or combine them with a comma.
DRIVER.SYS   Add a logical floppy drive.

 DEVICE=DRIVER.SYS /D:drive [/F:type] [/H:heads] [/S:sectors]
                   [/T:tracks] [/C]

   /D:drive        Physical drive number.
   /F:type         Drive format code.
   /H:heads        Head count.
   /S:sectors      Sectors per track.
   /T:tracks       Tracks per side.
   /C              Enable change-line support.
DRIVPARM=    Override disk drive parameters.

 DRIVPARM=/D:drive [/F:type] [/H:heads] [/S:sectors] [/T:tracks] [/C]

   /D:drive        Physical drive number.
   /F:type         Drive format code, through 7.
   /H:heads        Head count.
   /S:sectors      Sectors per track.
   /T:tracks       Tracks per side.
   /C              Enable change-line support.
ECHO         Control batch echoing or print a message.

 ECHO [ON|OFF|message]

   ON, OFF         Show or hide commands as a batch file runs.
   message         Text to display.
EDIT         Create or change a text file in the full-screen editor.

 EDIT filename

   filename        Text file to open or create.

 Requires a PC text display.
EDLIN        Edit a text file.

 EDLIN filename [/B]

   filename        Text file to edit.
   /B              Ignore embedded Ctrl+Z characters.
EMM386.SYS   Manage expanded memory on a 386.

 DEVICE=EMM386.SYS [size] [Mx] [ON | OFF | AUTO]

   size            Expanded memory size in KB.
   Mx              Select the page-frame mapping.
   ON, OFF         Enable or disable expanded memory.
   AUTO            Enable expanded memory on demand.
ERASE        Delete one or more files.

 ERASE [drive:][path]filename [/P] [/Q]

   filename        File or wildcard pattern to delete.
   /P              Ask before deleting each file.
   /Q              Skip the bulk deletion prompt.
EXE2BIN      Convert an eligible EXE image to binary form.

 EXE2BIN input [output]

   input           Executable file to convert.
   output          Output filename.
EXIT         Leave the current command interpreter.

 EXIT
FASTOPEN     Cache file and directory lookups.

 FASTOPEN drive:[=names | =(names,extents)] ... [/X]

   drive           Local fixed drive to cache.
   names           File and directory entries (10-999).
   extents         File extent entries. Omitting both counts uses 48 each.
   /X              Use expanded memory for the cache.
FC           Compare two files and display their differences.

 FC [/A] [/B] [/C] [/L] [/LBn] [/N] [/T] [/W] [/Dcount] file1 file2

   file1, file2    Files to compare.
   /A              Show shorter difference groups.
   /B              Compare bytes.
   /C              Ignore case.
   /L              Compare text lines.
   /LBn            Buffer n text lines.
   /N              Show line numbers.
   /T              Preserve tabs.
   /W              Ignore whitespace and skip blank lines.
   /Dcount         Resume after count matching lines (default 2).
                   Alias: /number. Switch letters ignore case.
FCBS=        Set the number of file control blocks.

 FCBS=n,m [/L]

   n               Number of file control blocks.
   m               Blocks protected from automatic closure.
   /L              Keep the FCB table in conventional memory.
FDISK        Manage fixed-disk partitions.

 FDISK [/STATUS]
 FDISK /MBR
 FDISK disk [/PRI:size] [/EXT:size] [/LOG:size] [/Q]

   /STATUS         Show disk usage.
   /MBR            Rewrite disk 1's master boot code. A missing 55AAh signature
                   clears the partition table.
   disk            Disk number, starting at 1.
   /PRI, /EXT      Create a primary or extended DOS partition (MB).
   /LOG            Create a logical drive in the extended partition.
   /Q              Skip the reboot prompt.
FILES=       Set the maximum number of open files.

 FILES=count [/L]

   count           Maximum open files.
   /L              Keep the file table in conventional memory (Windows 3.0).
FIND         Search for text in files or standard input.

 FIND [/V] [/C] [/N] [/I] "text" [files...]

   "text"          String to search for.
   files           Files to search. Omit to read standard input.
   /V              Display nonmatching lines.
   /C              Count matching lines.
   /N              Include line numbers.
   /I              Ignore case.

 ERRORLEVEL is 0 if the string occurs, 1 if absent, or 2 on error.
FOR          Run a command for each item in a set.

 FOR %v IN (set) DO command

   %v              Current item. Use %%v in batch files.
   set             Names or patterns to process.
   command         Command to run for each item.
FORMAT       Prepare a disk for DOS.

 FORMAT drive: [/Q] [/V[:label]] [/S] [/B] [/F:size]
               [/T:tracks /N:sectors] [/1] [/4] [/8]

   drive           Disk to format.
   /Q              Quick format.
   /V[:label]      Set the volume label.
   /S              Transfer DOS system files.
   /B              Reserve space for DOS system files.
   /F:size         Select floppy capacity.
   /T:tracks       Tracks per side.
   /N:sectors      Sectors per track.
   /1              Format one side.
   /4              Format 360 KB in a high-density drive.
   /8              Use eight sectors per track.
GOTO         Continue a batch file at the named label.

 GOTO label

   label           Target label. Define it as :label at the start of a line.
GRAFTABL     Load or identify a graphics character table.

 GRAFTABL [codepage | /STATUS | /STA | ?]

   codepage        Character table (default 437).
                     437  USA               850  Multilingual
                     860  Portuguese        863  Canadian French
                     865  Nordic
   /STATUS, /STA   Display the loaded table.
   ?               List supported parameters and code pages.
GRAPHICS     Enable printing of graphics screens.

 GRAPHICS [type] [/R] [/B] [/LCD] [/PRINTBOX:name | /PB:name]

   type            Printer type.
   /R              Reverse the printed image.
   /B              Include the background.
   /LCD            Select the LCD screen.
   /PRINTBOX:name  Select a print box. Short form: /PB:name.
GWBASIC      Run a BASIC program or start the interactive editor.

 GWBASIC [filename] [/NOB[ANNER]] [/NOR[UN]] [/M:n] [/C:n] [/F:n] [/S:n]

   filename        Load and run the program. Omit it for the Ok prompt.
   /NOB[ANNER]     Hide the banner, free-byte count, and function-key labels.
   /NOR[UN]        Load the program and wait at the Ok prompt. RUN starts it.
   /M:n            Set the data segment limit in bytes (decimal or &H hex).
   /C:n            Set the serial buffer size in bytes.
   /F:n, /S:n      Accepted. Files and records are allocated dynamically.

   Options may precede or follow the filename. Type SYSTEM to return to DOS.
   Example: GWBASIC /NOB DEMO.BAS /NOR
HELP         List help topics or read about one topic.

 HELP [topic]

   topic           Command, driver or CONFIG.SYS directive to look up.

 Omit the topic to browse the index. Use /? on supported commands
 to display the same help page.
HIMEM.SYS    Manage extended memory on an AT-compatible 286 or later.

 DEVICE=[drive:][path]HIMEM.SYS

   DOS=HIGH        Load selected DOS routines into the high memory area.

 Example for DOS installed in C:\DOS:
   DOS=HIGH
   DEVICE=C:\DOS\HIMEM.SYS

 For upper memory too, use DOS=HIGH,UMB and load UMBS.SYS after HIMEM.SYS.
 See HELP UMBS.SYS for the memory ranges.
IF           Run a batch command when a condition is true.

 IF [NOT] ERRORLEVEL number command
 IF [NOT] string1==string2 command
 IF [NOT] EXIST filename command
 IF [NOT] DIREXIST path command

   NOT             Reverse the test result.
   ERRORLEVEL      True if exit status is at least number.
   EXIST           True if the file exists.
   DIREXIST        True if the directory exists.
INSTALL=     Run an executable during configuration.

 INSTALL=program [arguments]

   program         Executable to run during CONFIG.SYS processing.
JOIN         Join a drive to a directory or undo it.

 JOIN [drive: path | drive: /D]

   drive           Drive to attach to a directory.
   path            Directory to attach the drive to.
   /D              Remove the join.
KEYB         Select a keyboard layout.

 KEYB [layout[,codepage[,file]]] [/ID:id] [/E]

   layout          Keyboard layout code.
   codepage        Code page to use with the layout.
   file            Keyboard definition file.
   /ID:id          Select the keyboard by ID.
   /E              Assume an enhanced keyboard when installing on XT or AT.
KEYBOARD.SYS Keyboard layout data used by KEYB.

 KEYB layout[,codepage[,file]]

   file            Keyboard definition file read by KEYB.
LABEL        Display, set, or remove a disk volume label.

 LABEL [drive:] [label]

   drive           Volume to label.
   label           New volume label (up to 11 bytes). Omit it for a prompt.
LASTDRIVE=   Set the highest drive letter.

 LASTDRIVE=letter

   letter          Highest drive letter DOS should allocate.
LH           Alias for LOADHIGH. Run a program in upper memory when available.

 LH program [arguments]

   program         External command to run.
LOADFIX      Run a program above the first 64 KiB.

 LOADFIX program [arguments]

   program         Executable to load above the first 64 KB.
LOADHIGH     Run an external program in upper memory when available.

 LOADHIGH program [arguments]
 LH program [arguments]

   program         External command to run.
MD           Create a directory.

 MD [drive:]path

   path            Directory to create.
MEM          Show memory usage, optionally with paging.

 MEM [/C | /CLASSIFY | /D | /DEBUG] [/P]

   /C, /CLASSIFY   Classify memory use by program.
   /D, /DEBUG      Display detailed memory information.
   /P              Pause after each screen.
MKDIR        Create a directory.

 MKDIR [drive:]path

   path            Directory to create.
MODE         Configure the console, serial ports, printers and code pages.

 MODE [device] /STATUS       Device status. Short forms: /STAT, /STA.
 MODE                        Status of all devices.
 MODE CON [COLS=c] [LINES=n] [RATE=r] [DELAY=d]
   40 or 80 columns. 25, 43 or 50 lines, adapter permitting.
   Repeat rate 1 (slow) to 32 (fast). Delay in quarter-seconds (1-4).
 MODE {40|80|BW40|BW80|CO40|CO80|MONO} [,L|R][,T]
   L/R shifts the image left/right. T tests the adjustment.
 MODE COMn [BAUD=b] [PARITY=p] [DATA=d] [STOP=s] [RETRY=r]
   COM1-COM4. MODE COM1:9600,N,8,1 selects 9600 baud, no parity, 8 data bits
   and 1 stop bit. M/S parity and 19200 baud depend on hardware.
 MODE LPTn [COLS=c] [LINES=n] [RETRY=r]
   LPT1-LPT3. 80/132 columns, 6/8 lines per inch. Example: MODE LPT1:80,6
 MODE LPTn:=COMm             Redirect printer output to COMm.
 MODE LPTn:                  Cancel redirection.
 MODE device CP PREP=((pages) filename)   Load pages from a CPI file.
 MODE device CP SEL=page                  Activate a prepared page.
 MODE device CP REFRESH                   Reload the active page.
 MODE device CP /STATUS                   List code-page information.
   Use CON or a code-page printer. Example: MODE CON CP SEL=850
MORE         Page a text file or piped input.

 MORE [filename]

   filename        Text file to page. Omit to read standard input.

 Example: DIR /S | MORE
MOVE         Move files or rename a directory.

 MOVE [/Y | /-Y] source[,source...] destination

   source          File, pattern or directory. Separate sources with commas.
   destination     New name or destination directory.
   /Y              Suppress confirmation.
   /-Y             Prompt before overwriting.
MULTITRACK=  Configure multitrack disk I/O.

 MULTITRACK=ON
 MULTITRACK=OFF
NLSFUNC      Load national-language support.

 NLSFUNC [filename]

   filename        Country data file path.
PATH         Display or set the executable search path.

 PATH [directory[;directory...]]

   directory       Directory to search for external commands.

 Run PATH alone to show the search path. PATH ; clears it.
PAUSE        Suspend batch execution until a key is pressed.

 PAUSE
PRINT        Queue files for printing or manage the print queue.

 PRINT [files...] [/D:device] [/B:size] [/Q:count] [/S:ticks]
       [/U:ticks] [/M:ticks] [/T] [/C] [/P]

   files           Files to queue.
   /D:device       Output device.
   /B:size         Print buffer size.
   /Q:count        Maximum files in queue.
   /S:ticks        Scheduling interval.
   /U:ticks        Busy-printer wait.
   /M:ticks        Maximum printing time slice.
   /T              Cancel the whole queue.
   /C              Cancel listed files.
   /P              Queue listed files.
PRINTER.SYS  Install printer code-page support.

 DEVICE=PRINTER.SYS LPT#[:]=(type[,hwcp[,n]])

   type            Printer type.
   hwcp            Hardware code page or a parenthesized list of code pages.
   n               Number of software code-page slots.
PROMPT       Change the command prompt.

 PROMPT [text]

   text            Prompt text and codes. $P shows the path and $G prints >.
RAMDRIVE.SYS Create a RAM disk.

 DEVICE=RAMDRIVE.SYS [KB] [sector-size] [entries] [/E | /A | /U]

   KB              Disk size in KiB.
   sector-size     Bytes per sector.
   entries         Root entries.
   /E              XMS. Load HIMEM.SYS first.
   /A              EMS.
   /U              AT&T 6300 PLUS upper extended memory.
RD           Remove an empty directory.

 RD [drive:]path

   path            Empty directory to remove.
RECOVER      Recover readable data from a file or disk.

 RECOVER filename
 RECOVER drive:

   filename        File to recover readable data from.
   drive           Disk to process.
REM          Add a comment to a batch file.

 REM [text]

   text            Batch file comment.
REN          Rename files.

 REN [drive:][path]oldname newname

   oldname         File or wildcard pattern to rename.
   newname         New filename or pattern.
RENAME       Rename files.

 RENAME [drive:][path]oldname newname

   oldname         File or wildcard pattern to rename.
   newname         New filename or pattern.
REPLACE      Replace files in a destination directory.

 REPLACE source [destination] [/A] [/P] [/R] [/S] [/U] [/W]

   source          Files to copy.
   destination     Directory to update.
   /A              Add missing files.
   /P              Prompt for each file.
   /R              Replace read-only files.
   /S              Search destination subdirectories.
   /U              Replace older files only.
   /W              Wait for a disk before starting.
RESTORE      Restore files from a backup.

 RESTORE source-drive: [destination] [/S] [/P] [/M] [/N] [/D]
         [/B:date] [/A:date] [/E:time] [/L:time]

   source-drive    Backup drive.
   destination     Files or directory to restore.
   /S              Include subdirectories.
   /P              Prompt before restoring.
   /M              Select modified files.
   /N              Select missing destination files.
   /D              List matches without restoring.
   Dates take four-digit years.
   /B:date         On or before date.
   /A:date         On or after date.
   /E:time         At or before time.
   /L:time         At or after time.
RMDIR        Remove an empty directory.

 RMDIR [drive:]path

   path            Empty directory to remove.
SELECT       Run the DOS setup utility.

 SELECT MENU

   MENU            Start interactive installation from drive A.

 SELECT.COM prompts for the installation disk and starts SELECT.EXE.
 SELECT.EXE MENU starts the installer directly.

 Choose the option to omit MS-DOS Shell when using the project disk images.
SET          Display or change environment variables.

 SET [name=[value]]

   name            Environment variable to change.
   value           New value. Leave empty to remove the variable.

 Run SET alone to list environment variables.
SHARE        Install file sharing and locking support.

 SHARE [/F:bytes] [/L:locks] [/NC]

   /F:bytes        Reserve space for file-sharing information.
   /L:locks        Set the lock limit.
   /NC             Disable sharing checks.
SHELL=       Select the command interpreter and its arguments.

 SHELL=program [arguments]

   program         Startup command interpreter.
   arguments       Interpreter options.
SHELLHIGH=   Load the shell and permanent environment in upper memory.

 SHELLHIGH=program [arguments]

   program         Command interpreter to load high if possible.
   arguments       Interpreter options.

 DOS also tries to place the permanent environment in upper memory.
SHIFT        Shift the batch positional arguments.

 SHIFT
SMARTDRV.SYS Cache hard-disk reads.

 DEVICE=SMARTDRV.SYS [KB] [/A]

   KB              Cache size, 128 to 8192 KiB.
   /A              Use EMS. The default requires XMS (e.g. HIMEM.SYS).
SORT         Sort input.

 SORT [/R] [/+column]

   /R              Reverse the sort order.
   /+column        Compare starting at this column.
STACKS=      Configure interrupt stacks.

 STACKS=count,size [/L]

   count           Number of interrupt stacks.
   size            Bytes reserved per stack.
   /L              Keep interrupt stacks and handlers in conventional memory.
SUBST        Map a drive or remove its mapping.

 SUBST [drive: path | drive: /D]

   drive           Drive letter to assign.
   path            Directory represented by the drive letter.
   /D              Remove the mapping.
SWITCHES=    Configure DOS startup switches.

 SWITCHES=/K

   /K              Use conventional keyboard handling.
SYS          Transfer DOS system files to a disk.

 SYS [source] drive:

   source          Drive or path containing the DOS system files.
   drive           Disk to receive the system files.
TIME         Display or set the time.

 TIME [time]

   time            New system time.
TREE         Display a directory tree.

 TREE [drive:][path] [/F] [/A] [/L]

   path            Starting directory.
   /F              Include filenames.
   /A              Draw ASCII branches.
   /L              Display directory names in lowercase.
TRUENAME     Display the canonical path for a file or directory.

 TRUENAME [path]

   path            File or directory name to expand.
TYPE         Display a text file.

 TYPE [drive:][path]filename

   filename        Text file to send to standard output.
UMBS.SYS     Supply mapped RAM as upper memory blocks.

 DEVICE=UMBS.SYS start-end [...]

   start-end       Mapped memory range in hexadecimal segment addresses.
   end             First segment beyond the range.

 Separate additional ranges with spaces. Use only unused, mapped RAM.
 When using HIMEM.SYS, load it first. Load UMBS.SYS before DEVICEHIGH.
VDISK.SYS    Create a RAM disk.

 DEVICE=VDISK.SYS [KB] [sector-size] [entries] [/E[:n] | /X[:n]]

   KB              Disk size (default 64 KiB).
   sector-size     Bytes per sector (default 128).
   entries         Root entries (default 64).
   /E              Use XMS (load HIMEM.SYS first).
   /X              Use a DOS-reserved EMS page.
   n               Transfer 1 to 8 sectors (default 8).
VER          Display the DOS version.

 VER
VERIFY       Control verification of disk writes.

 VERIFY [ON|OFF]

   ON, OFF         Enable or disable verification of disk writes.
VOL          Display the disk volume label.

 VOL [drive:]

   drive           Volume to identify.
XCOPY        Copy files and directory trees.

 XCOPY source [destination] [/A | /M] [/D:date] [/P] [/S] [/E] [/V] [/W]

   source          Files or directory to copy.
   destination     Target drive, directory or file.
   /A              Copy archive-marked files. Keep the bit set.
   /M              Copy archive-marked files and clear the bit.
   /D:date         Copy files changed on or after date (four-digit year).
   /P              Prompt for each file.
   /S              Copy nonempty subdirectories.
   /E              With /S, include empty subdirectories.
   /V              Verify writes.
   /W              Wait for a key before copying.

 XCOPYCMD sets defaults. /-S and /-E cancel preset switches.
XMA2EMS.SYS  Provide EMS services using XMA memory.

 DEVICE=XMA2EMS.SYS
XMAEM.SYS    Emulate XMA on supported hardware.

 DEVICE=XMAEM.SYS [KB]

   KB              Emulated memory size in KB.
